      "FANNY: Unwrap it.\nFANNY: Read it.\nMARGARET: ENDYMION BOOK 1 “A thing of beauty is a joy for ever: Its loveliness increases; it will never Pass into nothingness; but still will keep A b…\nMARGARET: “Spite of despondence, of the inhuman dearth”",
      "MARGARET: I want to go. I want to leave. It smells.\nFANNY: Shush, or I’ll cut your hair in the night.",
      "MARIA DILKE: In this house we do not acknowledge it.\nFANNY: Was it so very bad?\nMARIA DILKE: I can’t bring myself to remember...",
